    "result_text": "All 281 tests pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`. (The `ERROR GeneralExceptionHandler - Unexpected error` line is expected output from a test exercising the error-handling path, not a failure.)\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreation.java`:\n- Uses a dedicated SLF4J logger named `\"AUDIT\"`.\n- Reads the authenticated user from `SecurityContextHolder` (falling back to `\"anonymous\"`), and logs it together with the new owner's `id` and `membershipNumber` via `@Val Owner`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (under the same `transaction` governance), so it runs only after a successful save when the owner id has been assigned.\n\nPlacing it after `SaveOwner` ensures the id is populated, and after `AssignMembershipNumber` ensures the membership number is present. The cp19 acceptance test confirms the log line `Owner created by user=acceptance-admin id=11 membershipNumber=11`, and the full suite remains green.",
